lifeos-nix patch f-mergesettings-hooks-overlay — compose a USER hooks overlay so our
hook additions never live inside the official hooks.json

PROBLEM
  Our custom hooks (TelosSummarySync, the codeberg statusline auto-update, an extra
  DocIntegrity) were added by EDITING the official hooks/hooks.json in place. Mixed
  ownership means every upstream hooks.json evolution collides with our edits — the file
  is permanently "ours-modified official" (a B∩C case) and can never sync cleanly.

FIX (1 file, MergeSettings.ts)
  After re-attaching the official hooks (b), compose a USER overlay at
  LIFEOS/USER/CONFIG/hooks.user.json (the ours-zone, alongside PULSE.user.toml) — unioned
  per event onto the official entries. hooks/hooks.json stays PURE official → syncs cleanly,
  no collision. Missing overlay = official only (fresh install, no-op). Malformed overlay =
  abort loud (never compose a broken hooks block). Mirrors the settings.system/settings.user
  split. No new imports (path/os/existsSync/parseJsonFileOrThrow/isObjectRecord already used).

--- a/LifeOS/install/LIFEOS/TOOLS/MergeSettings.ts
+++ b/LifeOS/install/LIFEOS/TOOLS/MergeSettings.ts
@@ -568,6 +568,26 @@
     }
     merged.hooks = hooksJson.hooks;
 
+    // (b2) Compose the USER hooks overlay over the official base. Our hook additions live
+    // in LIFEOS/USER/CONFIG/hooks.user.json (the ours-zone, alongside PULSE.user.toml) —
+    // NEVER mixed into the official hooks.json, which then stays pure-official and syncs
+    // cleanly (no per-update B∩C collision). Overlay entries are unioned per event onto the
+    // official ones. Missing overlay = official only (fresh install, no-op). Malformed overlay
+    // = abort loud rather than compose a broken hooks block. Mirrors the settings.user.json split.
+    const hooksOverlayPath = path.join(os.homedir(), ".claude", "LIFEOS", "USER", "CONFIG", "hooks.user.json");
+    if (existsSync(hooksOverlayPath)) {
+      const overlay = await parseJsonFileOrThrow(hooksOverlayPath);
+      if (!isObjectRecord(overlay?.hooks)) {
+        throw new Error(`hooks overlay ${hooksOverlayPath} has no valid .hooks object — refusing to compose a broken hooks block.`);
+      }
+      const composed = merged.hooks as Record<string, unknown[]>;
+      for (const [event, entries] of Object.entries(overlay.hooks as Record<string, unknown>)) {
+        if (!Array.isArray(entries)) continue;
+        composed[event] = Array.isArray(composed[event]) ? [...composed[event], ...entries] : [...entries];
+      }
+      merged.hooks = composed;
+    }
+
     // The harness exports env values verbatim — expand leading $HOME/${HOME}/~ so
     // LIFEOS_DIR et al. resolve to real paths on a fresh install (#1404 / #1422).
     expandEnvHomeReferences(merged, process.env.HOME || "");
